to places like Cannes

236
00:10:35,118 --> 00:10:37,067
in the biggest party
season of the year

237
00:10:37,331 --> 00:10:39,161
where girls roam the streets topless.

238
00:10:39,912 --> 00:10:41,053
Maybe it's a missionary trip

239
00:10:41,134 --> 00:10:43,437
and they're there
to convince the girls to cover up.

240
00:10:43,599 --> 00:10:44,644
Maybe.

241
00:10:45,102 --> 00:10:46,421
- Oh, Jesus.
- What?

242
00:10:46,525 --> 00:10:49,063
I'm fine with the nuns.
It's this guy that scares me.

243
00:10:49,307 --> 00:10:51,094
No profiling, Turtle.
I don't believe it.

244
00:10:51,236 --> 00:10:53,472
Have you seen <i>24</i>?
'Cause I have.

245
00:10:56,123 --> 00:10:58,255
- All right, let's make a move.
- What kind of move?

246
00:10:58,823 --> 00:11:00,224
The same kind of move I made

247
00:11:00,265 --> 00:11:02,437
when I was terrified
of Pete Minetto in high school...

248
00:11:02,519 --> 00:11:03,922
we befriend him,
make him love us.

249
00:11:03,983 --> 00:11:06,637
That way when he seizes the plane
and starts executing people

250
00:11:07,489 --> 00:11:08,566
he let's us go free.

251
00:11:08,687 --> 00:11:10,124
I don't want to befriend him.

252
00:11:11,464 --> 00:11:13,352
Then I'm gonna feel
no guilt if I survive.

253
00:11:17,681 --> 00:11:19,326
Are these seats taken, my friend?

254
00:11:20,178 --> 00:11:21,255
Great.

255
00:11:23,468 --> 00:11:25,255
I'm Johnny.
This is Turtle.

256
00:11:25,714 --> 00:11:26,912
Oh, and this is Ari.

257
00:11:30,596 --> 00:11:31,835
Ari's fucked.

258
00:11:33,140 --> 00:11:34,866
I'm an actor.
What do you do?

259
00:11:35,317 --> 00:11:37,286
I'm fine.
I don't know what you're talking about.

260
00:11:37,368 --> 00:11:39,621
If you're fine, why are
you out shopping for cars?

261
00:11:39,831 --> 00:11:41,679
What does one thing
have to do with the other?

262
00:11:41,740 --> 00:11:44,298
I want a new car. What, I can't
have a new car if I want one?

263
00:11:44,378 --> 00:11:46,327
- It's my money also.
- You can have a new car.

264
00:11:46,388 --> 00:11:48,255
I'm saying you might want to go home

265
00:11:48,296 --> 00:11:50,753
because there are probably
beautiful flowers waiting for you.

266
00:11:50,814 --> 00:11:52,913
Why?
Are you feeling guilty about something?

267
00:11:53,137 --> 00:11:56,828
I'm not feeling guilty, baby. You're
happy. You're fine with not going.

268
00:11:56,990 --> 00:11:58,289
And you're happy I'm not going.

269
00:11:59,365 --> 00:12:00,644
How much are the Mybachs?

270
00:12:00,887 --> 00:12:01,945
I'll call you back, Ari.

271
00:12:02,087 --> 00:12:04,361
<i>Please check the board for rescheduling.</i>

272
00:12:05,413 --> 00:12:06,489
FLIGHT CANCELED

273
00:12:06,550 --> 00:12:08,256
You gotta be shitting me.

274
00:12:11,260 --> 00:12:13,229
- Baby...
- This is not your baby.

275
00:12:13,351 --> 00:12:15,077
This is your
underappreciated assistant.

276
00:12:15,341 --> 00:12:17,595
- What do you want, Lloyd?
- I spoke to my therapist

277
00:12:17,813 --> 00:12:19,803
and he said I should not
hide what I'm feeling.

278
00:12:19,925 --> 00:12:23,092
I should express to you my hurt
and disappointment about not going.

279
00:12:23,214 --> 00:12:24,722
Well, now that you've
expressed that,

280
00:12:24,783 --> 00:12:27,626
let me express my frustration
that my flight has been canceled.

281
00:12:28,072 --> 00:12:31,176
Maybe this is karma.
Perhaps you should do something

282
00:12:31,257 --> 00:12:33,186
to turn it before something
really bad happens.

283
00:12:33,308 --> 00:12:34,937
Today, Lloyd?
Under code red?

284
00:12:35,404 --> 00:12:36,825
I'm sorry, Ari.
That was wrong.

285
00:12:37,028 --> 00:12:38,311
Yeah, it was.
Now listen,

286
00:12:38,453 --> 00:12:41,113
call my boy Kenny Dichter
over at Marquis Jets,

287
00:12:41,255 --> 00:12:43,468
see if me and the boys
can hop on a flight today.

288
00:12:43,651 --> 00:12:45,559
- You're gonna fly private?
- Just do it.

289
00:12:46,392 --> 00:12:50,026
Maybe in France we'll hit the
restaurant of your choice, on us.

290
00:12:50,188 --> 00:12:52,440
The flight's canceled.
Let's get the hell out of here.

291
00:12:52,603 --> 00:12:54,613
Really?
That's awesome.

292
00:12:56,176 --> 00:12:57,706
How do I get in touch with you?

293
00:12:58,579 --> 00:13:00,375
You don't.
If it's meant to be

294
00:13:00,619 --> 00:13:02,649
we'll run into each other.
Be well, my friend.

295
00:13:03,815 --> 00:13:05,785
That girl is wife material...

296
00:13:05,886 --> 00:13:08,275
wife, mother,
grow-old-together material.

297
00:13:08,377 --> 00:13:09,575
Too bad you have a girlfriend.

298
00:13:09,576 --> 00:13:11,524
Yeah. You did promise
you wouldn't hit on her.

299
00:13:11,727 --> 00:13:14,016
I'm talking in terms
of presence for the film.

300
00:13:14,300 --> 00:13:16,107
The sister has to have that thing

301
00:13:16,229 --> 00:13:18,662
that you just adore at all
times in order for her to be able

302
00:13:18,723 --> 00:13:21,240
to get away with some of
the more vicious things that she does.

303
00:13:21,322 --> 00:13:23,447
Speaking of which,
you could have come to my defense

304
00:13:23,508 --> 00:13:25,528
just a little when she was
quizzing me back there.

305
00:13:25,569 --> 00:13:26,584
- Your defense?
- Yeah,

306
00:13:26,625 --> 00:13:28,049
she asked me pretty tough questions,

307
00:13:28,090 --> 00:13:30,100
you're just sitting there
like you got no tongue.

308
00:13:30,161 --> 00:13:32,617
You were talking the whole time.
What did you want me to say?

309
00:13:32,678 --> 00:13:34,771
She looked at you a couple
of times for reassurance

310
00:13:34,791 --> 00:13:37,431
- and you didn't give her much.
- 'Cause it's an awkward position.

311
00:13:37,512 --> 00:13:39,441
I'm her manager but I'm
also a producer on this.

312
00:13:39,552 --> 00:13:41,503
It's a no-show-type job title anyway.

313
00:13:42,192 --> 00:13:43,723
I don't want to jam it down her throat.

314
00:13:43,743 --> 00:13:45,916
Plus, it doesn't really matter.
She's got the script,

315
00:13:45,977 --> 00:13:47,885
she loved Billy,
so what do you want me to say?

316
00:13:47,967 --> 00:13:49,341
You think she loved me, suit?

317
00:13:50,722 --> 00:13:53,256
- Hey, what's up, Turtle?
- <i>Yo, E, our flight's canceled.</i>

318
00:13:53,392 --> 00:13:55,431
- What?
- The whole airport's shut down.

319
00:13:55,694 --> 00:13:57,562
All right,
we'll meet you back at the house.

320
00:13:58,192 --> 00:14:00,536
L.A.X. is closed.
There's no flights leaving today.

321
00:14:01,185 --> 00:14:02,241
- Jesus.
- What?

322
00:14:02,935 --> 00:14:05,047
I couldn't bear
going without you, baby.

323
00:14:05,148 --> 00:14:07,625
I know they closed the airport.
It's all over the news,

324
00:14:07,727 --> 00:14:09,981
so stop making it
like it's some grand gesture.

325
00:14:10,062 --> 00:14:13,031
Baby, what did we learn about
being passive-aggressive in therapy?

326
00:14:13,214 --> 00:14:16,359
If you wanted to go you should
have not said "I don't want to go."

327
00:14:16,989 --> 00:14:18,638
I'm tired of feeling
like I'm not wanted.

328
00:14:18,699 --> 00:14:21,279
Baby, what are you talking about?
This is a one-time thing.

329
00:14:21,745 --> 00:14:23,248
You came home last night
and you said

330
00:14:23,288 --> 00:14:25,502
that the hotel had screwed us
out of a king-sized bed

331
00:14:25,542 --> 00:14:27,513
and would I
"really be comfortable in a single?"

332
00:14:27,574 --> 00:14:29,391
<i>and then this morning
before the news came on</i>

333
00:14:29,431 --> 00:14:31,218
<i>you said that Brian Sher's wife
wasn't going</i>

334
00:14:31,299 --> 00:14:33,666
and if she found out
that I was going, she would go crazy.

335
00:14:33,768 --> 00:14:36,764
There are some men that would kill to go
to the south of France with me

336
00:14:36,825 --> 00:14:38,124
<i>and if you're not one of them...</i>

337
00:14:38,185 --> 00:14:41,067
I am one of them, honey.
I'm glad that the flight was canceled,

338
00:14:41,209 --> 00:14:43,402
so now I can tell you I want you to go.

339
00:14:43,787 --> 00:14:45,470
<i>I don't want to go without you</i>

340
00:14:45,713 --> 00:14:48,353
and I love you.
Now will you go?

341
00:14:48,697 --> 00:14:49,746
No, Ari, I won't.

342
00:14:50,104 --> 00:14:51,119
Why not?

343
00:14:51,301 --> 00:14:53,576
Well, because all that will
do is assuage your guilt.

344
00:14:54,541 --> 00:14:55,757
Why would you want to do that?

345
00:14:55,878 --> 00:14:58,698
- Well, you shouldn't feel guilty.
- What should I feel?

346
00:14:58,942 --> 00:15:00,424
Sadness that for some reason

347
00:15:00,505 --> 00:15:02,730
you're married to someone
you don't like to be with.

348
00:15:02,892 --> 00:15:05,790
Laura, I'll definitely
need some help upstairs.

349
00:15:06,898 --> 00:15:07,974
Hello, Lloyd.

350
00:15:08,859 --> 00:15:10,592
- Hello, Ari.
- You're not my mistress.

351
00:15:10,694 --> 00:15:12,486
Stop being mad at me.
- I'm no longer mad.

352
00:15:12,587 --> 00:15:14,861
You shouldn't be,
'cause I'd love to have you in Cannes.

353
00:15:14,902 --> 00:15:17,672
So go home, pack your favorite sarong
and consider yourself invited.

354
00:15:17,753 --> 00:15:19,592
- Are you serious?
- I'm so serious

355
00:15:19,774 --> 00:15:21,500
that I'm actually
embarrassed for myself.

356
00:15:21,581 --> 00:15:23,245
- That's very sweet of you.
- It's not,

357
00:15:23,286 --> 00:15:26,006
'cause I don't want to see you when
I'm there. This is a man's trip,

358
00:15:26,074 --> 00:15:28,084
so you're gonna have to
find your own dick clique.

359
00:15:28,165 --> 00:15:29,910
That is fine, Ari.
Oh my god.

360
00:15:30,337 --> 00:15:33,342
I'm so happy.
But how are we getting there?

361
00:15:33,545 --> 00:15:35,975
- You called Kenny D., right?
- He says there are no jets.

362
00:15:36,219 --> 00:15:39,102
The whole town is scrambling since
the alert and you scrambled too late.

363
00:15:39,224 --> 00:15:41,683
- There's not one more plane?
- There was one,

364
00:15:41,784 --> 00:15:43,355
but Sydney Pollack just booked it.

365
00:15:43,619 --> 00:15:44,756
Fuck!

366
00:15:45,121 --> 00:15:46,827
The airline said
that they can't guarantee

367
00:15:46,908 --> 00:15:49,097
that we can get on a flight tomorrow?
This is unreal.

368
00:15:49,178 --> 00:15:52,102
My travel lady says
we could drive to Phoenix,

369
00:15:52,183 --> 00:15:54,960
get on a flight to st. Louis and
then hop on a flight to France.

370
00:15:55,894 --> 00:15:57,641
- Sounds miserable.
- Beyond miserable.

371
00:15:57,762 --> 00:16:00,110
This is insane.
<i>Medellin</i> premieres in 48 hours.

372
00:16:00,212 --> 00:16:01,808
- We may not make it.
- We'll make it.

373
00:16:01,869 --> 00:16:03,636
Ari will take care of it, I'm sure.

374
00:16:04,367 --> 00:16:05,567
Hey, what's up, Anna?

375
00:16:05,668 --> 00:16:08,053
I thought you'd be on a plane.
I was gonna leave a message.

376
00:16:08,135 --> 00:16:10,023
No, everything got canceled.
Turn on the news.

377
00:16:10,124 --> 00:16:11,952
Oh, I'm sorry.
That sucks.

378
00:16:12,196 --> 00:16:13,292
What's going on?

379
00:16:13,719 --> 00:16:15,018
It's about Billy's script.

380
00:16:17,485 --> 00:16:18,602
Can I speak freely?

381
00:16:18,704 --> 00:16:20,186
Of course.
What's going on?

382
00:16:21,059 --> 00:16:22,318
I don't get it.

383
00:16:24,860 --> 00:16:27,633
It's Sydney Pollack returning.
My fingers are all crossed.

384
00:16:29,250 --> 00:16:30,783
Is this my dear old friend Sydney?

385
00:16:31,006 --> 00:16:33,372
I told you when I fired you
we weren't friends.

386
00:16:33,493 --> 00:16:36,616
You consider that a firing?
I like to look back at it

387
00:16:36,677 --> 00:16:38,789
as an amicable parting of the ways.

388
00:16:38,910 --> 00:16:41,515
I'm not coming back, okay?
You understand the word "never"?

389
00:16:41,698 --> 00:16:43,221
Well, you just keep thinking about it

390
00:16:43,282 --> 00:16:45,581
because this is not a business
call, this is personal.

391
00:16:45,845 --> 00:16:47,038
I need a lift to Cannes.

392
00:16:47,424 --> 00:16:49,312
<i>I heard you got the last plane
out of marquis</i>

393
00:16:49,393 --> 00:16:52,926
and I've got to get Vinnie Chase and
the <i>Medellin</i> crew there by tomorrow.

394
00:16:53,251 --> 00:16:55,815
<i>Medellin</i>... You know,
I hear a lot of hype about that film.

395
00:16:55,937 --> 00:16:57,724
It's phenomenal.
It's absolutely phenomenal.

396
00:16:57,843 --> 00:17:00,503
I'm not completely sold
on that kid of yours yet.

397
00:17:00,686 --> 00:17:04,010
After a plane ride and a screening
you'll see him as the next Redford.

398
00:17:04,274 --> 00:17:06,325
You want to do a
<i>Three Days of the Condor</i> sequel?

399
00:17:06,446 --> 00:17:07,563
No.

400
00:17:08,192 --> 00:17:09,634
I wouldn't mind reading him, though.

401
00:17:09,689 --> 00:17:12,248
You know, maybe something
would come up.

402
00:17:13,527 --> 00:17:15,517
<i>Okay, Ari, I'll give you a lift,</i>

403
00:17:15,840 --> 00:17:17,464
as long as I don't sit next to you.

404
00:17:17,528 --> 00:17:18,797
I'll ride in the bathroom.

405
00:17:19,345 --> 00:17:21,426
- <i>How many you got?</i>
- Six.

406
00:17:21,686 --> 00:17:25,382
I can't take six. I can do maybe five,
and that's gonna be tight.

407
00:17:25,686 --> 00:17:28,447
We'll make do. Listen,
I still love you, Sydney.

408
00:17:28,620 --> 00:17:31,158
6:30 sharp at Van Nuys.
Goodbye, Ari.

409
00:17:34,183 --> 00:17:35,496
Come on.
It was a numbers thing.

410
00:17:35,557 --> 00:17:37,344
You heard...
I couldn't have done anything.

411
00:17:37,425 --> 00:17:39,049
- Where are you doing?
- To unpack.

412
00:17:39,293 --> 00:17:41,514
Unpack?
You couldn't have even packed yet.

413
00:17:41,981 --> 00:17:45,128
In my mind, I did, Ari.
Iin my mind, I did.

414
00:17:45,672 --> 00:17:47,134
It's not my fault she doesn't get it.

415
00:17:47,195 --> 00:17:49,368
But it is your fault
if you don't try and help her to.

416
00:17:49,429 --> 00:17:52,245
- What do you want me to say?
- I want you to say that you're gonna go

417
00:17:52,286 --> 00:17:53,981
convince her
that she should do the movie,

418
00:17:54,062 --> 00:17:57,265
because that's what your director wants,
and as a producer, that is your job.

419
00:17:57,549 --> 00:17:58,553
It's your job, E.

420
00:17:58,675 --> 00:18:00,565
How would you like me
to try to convince her?

421
00:18:00,809 --> 00:18:02,615
Tell her how great
you think it's gonna be.

422
00:18:02,693 --> 00:18:03,871
That's what she wants to hear.

423
00:18:03,932 --> 00:18:05,662
What if I don't think
it's gonna be great?

424
00:18:05,743 --> 00:18:08,158
Should I lie to her?
'Cause that's not what a manager does.

425
00:18:08,361 --> 00:18:09,539
You lied to me.

426
00:18:10,520 --> 00:18:12,844
What, you don't think I know
you don't like it?

427
00:18:12,925 --> 00:18:14,818
I don't know,
you've never asked for my opinion

428
00:18:14,858 --> 00:18:17,335
- before you agreed to do the movie.
- Because you hate Billy.

429
00:18:17,396 --> 00:18:20,071
I knew there was no way you
were gonna read it with an open mind.

430
00:18:20,112 --> 00:18:21,391
What, you're a mind-reader now?

431
00:18:21,432 --> 00:18:23,273
You asked me if I thought it was okay

432
00:18:23,313 --> 00:18:25,871
if you sign Anna as a client
and I said one thing:

433
00:18:26,053 --> 00:18:28,147
"just make sure
it doesn't affect my career."

434
00:18:28,471 --> 00:18:29,730
This is the movie I'm making

435
00:18:29,795 --> 00:18:31,521
and this is who
I want to be in the movie.

436
00:18:31,562 --> 00:18:33,491
And I really believe
it's gonna be a great movie

437
00:18:33,531 --> 00:18:34,749
and she's gonna be great in it.

438
00:18:34,770 --> 00:18:36,906
You have to believe that
and try to make this happen.

439
00:18:36,946 --> 00:18:38,009
And if I can't?

440
00:18:38,043 --> 00:18:39,878
At least
make me believe that you tried.

441
00:18:40,371 --> 00:18:43,173
Hey, Ari called. He said we have
to be at the airport in three hours.

442
00:18:43,295 --> 00:18:44,312
How are we getting there?

443
00:18:44,332 --> 00:18:46,272
Sydney Pollack's
giving us a lift on his G-IV.

444
00:18:48,425 --> 00:18:49,582
Sweet.

445
00:18:49,721 --> 00:18:51,224
I told you it was gonna work out.

446
00:18:51,853 --> 00:18:53,071
It always does, right?

447
00:18:53,274 --> 00:18:55,602
- So do you really like the script?
- You really hate it?

448
00:18:55,988 --> 00:18:58,526
No, I don't hate it.
I'm unsure.

449
00:18:58,932 --> 00:19:00,365
You know, it's confusing.

450
00:19:00,812 --> 00:19:02,619
I'm really looking
for some guidance here.

451
00:19:02,971 --> 00:19:05,103
Yeah, well, maybe you
should give it another read.

452
00:19:07,296 --> 00:19:09,432
"Leopold furiously cooks breakfast.

453
00:19:09,696 --> 00:19:12,295
Curtis enters and Leopold,
overcome by his presence,

454
00:19:12,477 --> 00:19:14,672
sears his hand
over the hot sizzling bacon.

455
00:19:14,977 --> 00:19:16,357
Curtis begins to weep."

456
00:19:17,596 --> 00:19:19,589
- It's written in haiku.
- The guy's an original.

457
00:19:20,465 --> 00:19:22,556
I'm a little surprised
we're off on this.

458
00:19:22,922 --> 00:19:24,717
Maybe it's just
my head space right now.

459
00:19:24,920 --> 00:19:26,768
But if you think I should do it...

460
00:19:26,870 --> 00:19:29,187
do you think I should do it?
I really trust your opinion.

461
00:19:30,426 --> 00:19:32,131
I think Billy's gonna
make a great movie.

462
00:19:32,192 --> 00:19:34,189
So you were happy
with what he did on <i>Medellin</i>?

463
00:19:35,468 --> 00:19:36,767
It got into Cannes.

464
00:19:39,257 --> 00:19:40,821
Okay, I'll do it.

465
00:19:43,572 --> 00:19:45,663
I'm sure Billy and Vince
will be happy to hear that.

466
00:19:45,745 --> 00:19:47,167
So do you have to go to the airport?

467
00:19:47,309 --> 00:19:48,812
Yeah, the flight leaves at 6:30.

468
00:19:49,055 --> 00:19:51,411
Oh, you've got some time.
Do you want a drink?

